{"title":"Pedro Feijó de Moraes","markdown":{"yaml":{"title":"Pedro Feijó de Moraes","subtitle":"Ph.D. Candidate in Economics, Yale University","about":{"template":"trestles","image":"files/headshot.jpg","image-shape":"rounded","image-width":"13em","links":[{"icon":"file-earmark-pdf","text":"CV","href":"files/Feijo_de_Moraes_CV.pdf"},{"icon":"envelope","text":"Email","href":"mailto:pedro.feijodemoraes@yale.edu"},{"icon":"github","text":"GitHub","href":"https://github.com/PFeijodeMoraes23"},{"icon":"linkedin","text":"LinkedIn","href":"https://bit.ly/3qxJaco"}]}},"headingText":"Education","containsRefs":false,"markdown":"\n\nI am a Ph.D. candidate in Economics at Yale University, working in industrial\norganization and financial economics. My research studies competition in retail\nbanking: why depositors leave their money in low-yield accounts, and how much\nmarket power that inertia gives banks. I combine dynamic structural models of\ndemand with large administrative datasets from the Banco Central do Brasil.\n\nDuring my undergraduate studies, I spent a year as a macroeconomics research\nintern at Bahia Asset Management, where I ran GDP and CPI nowcasting models and\nmaintained the cross-country database used by the research team and the trading\ndesk. I hold an M.A. in Economics from FGV EPGE and placed first nationally in\nBrazil's 2019 ANPEC graduate entrance exam in economics.\n\nYou can reach me at [pedro.feijodemoraes@yale.edu](mailto:pedro.feijodemoraes@yale.edu).\n\n\n| | |\n|:--|--:|\n| **Ph.D., Economics**, Yale University | expected 2028 |\n| **M.Phil., M.A., Economics**, Yale University | 2025 |\n| **M.A., Economics**, FGV EPGE | 2021 |\n| **B.A., Economics**, FGV EPGE | 2018 |\n\n## Skills\n\n**Programming:** Python, Julia, R, MATLAB; Git, Bash, SLURM (HPC), LaTeX.<br>\n**Methods:** structural demand estimation (BLP), dynamic models, GMM and\ncontrol-function identification, panel econometrics.<br>\n**Languages:** Portuguese (native), English (fluent), Spanish and French (advanced).\n","srcMarkdownNoYaml":"\n\nI am a Ph.D. candidate in Economics at Yale University, working in industrial\norganization and financial economics. My research studies competition in retail\nbanking: why depositors leave their money in low-yield accounts, and how much\nmarket power that inertia gives banks. I combine dynamic structural models of\ndemand with large administrative datasets from the Banco Central do Brasil.\n\nDuring my undergraduate studies, I spent a year as a macroeconomics research\nintern at Bahia Asset Management, where I ran GDP and CPI nowcasting models and\nmaintained the cross-country database used by the research team and the trading\ndesk. I hold an M.A. in Economics from FGV EPGE and placed first nationally in\nBrazil's 2019 ANPEC graduate entrance exam in economics.\n\nYou can reach me at [pedro.feijodemoraes@yale.edu](mailto:pedro.feijodemoraes@yale.edu).\n\n## Education\n\n| | |\n|:--|--:|\n| **Ph.D., Economics**, Yale University | expected 2028 |\n| **M.Phil., M.A., Economics**, Yale University | 2025 |\n| **M.A., Economics**, FGV EPGE | 2021 |\n| **B.A., Economics**, FGV EPGE | 2018 |\n\n## Skills\n\n**Programming:** Python, Julia, R, MATLAB; Git, Bash, SLURM (HPC), LaTeX.<br>\n**Methods:** structural demand estimation (BLP), dynamic models, GMM and\ncontrol-function identification, panel econometrics.<br>\n**Languages:** Portuguese (native), English (fluent), Spanish and French (advanced).\n"},"formats":{"html":{"identifier":{"display-name":"HTML","target-format":"html","base-format":"html"},"execute":{"fig-width":7,"fig-height":5,"fig-format":"retina","fig-dpi":96,"df-print":"default","error":false,"eval":true,"cache":null,"freeze":false,"echo":true,"output":true,"warning":true,"include":true,"keep-md":false,"keep-ipynb":false,"ipynb":null,"enabled":null,"daemon":null,"daemon-restart":false,"debug":false,"ipynb-filters":[],"ipynb-shell-interactivity":null,"plotly-connected":true,"engine":"markdown"},"ren